{
  "_help": [
    "Every room and corridor is a rectangle of FLOOR tiles (x, y = top-left tile, w, h = size). Walls are generated around them automatically.",
    "Leave exactly 1 tile between neighbouring rooms/corridors: that tile becomes the shared wall, and doors are cut through it.",
    "w/h default to the size for the room's kind (see 'sizes'). Give w/h explicitly to override.",
    "Doors: side N/S/E/W, 'at' = tile offset along that side (omit to centre). Each door is 2 tiles wide.",
    "label is what players see. Change it freely. id is what tasks.json and 'vents' refer to (as F<floor>:<id>).",
    "Furniture and hiding spots come from 'furniture' (per kind) and are placed by code; pieces that would block a door or cut a room in half are skipped.",
    "Run `npm run map` to check the layout and print an ASCII preview of both floors.",
    "chatRooms: rooms where living players can chat with everyone else in the same room (Enter / the chat button)."
  ],
